# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# The site moved to a bilingual structure: Romanian at the root (it is 80% of
# search demand) and English under /en. These 301s carry the equity of the old
# English-only URLs, which are indexed, over to their new homes.

# Legacy URL from the previous site. It is still indexed and was being treated
# as a second, competing copy of the homepage.
/home              /                  301
/home/             /                  301
/index.html        /                  301

# Old English-only paths -> their /en equivalents.
/rooms             /en/rooms          301
/facility          /en/facilities     301
/facilities        /en/facilities     301
/about             /en/about          301
/gallery           /en/gallery        301

# /contact keeps its path and now serves the Romanian page; the English
# version lives at /en/contact and the two reference each other via hreflang.

# No catch-all rule on purpose. Without one, Cloudflare Pages serves
# 404.html with a real 404 status, so unknown URLs stop being indexable
# duplicates of the homepage.
